    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“Just a little to the left, away from tragedy.”</em></p><p>When a creature you can see within <strong>6 squares</strong> makes an attack roll against a target that is <strong>bloodied</strong> (at or below half its Integrity), you can use your <strong>reaction</strong> to nudge the intention sideways.</p><ul><li>The attacker rerolls the lowest die on a contested check (such as a shove, grapple, or disarm) they immediately substitute in place of that attack, or may choose to apply the attack rolling 3d10 and keeping the lowest 2</strong> but automatically treat it as non-lethal.</li></ul><p>This is a narrative tool: you pivot a kill into a capture, a slam into a pin, a swing into a warning blow.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
